      "text": "funds funds pub. corp. bank fin corp\nIssuer govt\n(EBFs) (SSFs)\n1 Budget. central govt 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n2 Extra-budget. funds 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n3 Social security funds 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n4 State govt. 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n5 Local govt. 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 1123,
      "end_char": 1252,
      "text": "6 Nonfin pub. corp. 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n7 Central bank 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n8 Oth. pub. fin. corp 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\nTotal 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1252,
      "end_char": 1394,
      "text": "Staff Commentary: The classification of Mexico’s fiscal accounts in this SRDSA matches that used in the IMF’s Fiscal Monitor. State and Local\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1394,
      "end_char": 1538,
      "text": "governments are excluded from debt coverage given limits on their debt carrying capacity and the absence of the legal obligation on the part of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1538,
      "end_char": 1680,
      "text": "the Federal government to guarantee or assume their debt. Staff are not aware of data on accounts payables, although the relevant information\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1680,
      "end_char": 1818,
      "text": "is assumed to be included in other data used in this assessment. Debt is not consolidated across the Federal government and Non-Financial\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1818,
      "end_char": 1973,
      "text": "Public Sector and the aggregate debt data represents the gross amount of all individual debt liabilities.\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 57\nSPFN\ndetcepxe\n:GG\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 1973,
      "end_char": 2176,
      "text": "1/ CG=Central government; GG=General government; NFPS=Nonfinancial public sector; PS=Public sector.\n2/ Stock of arrears could be used as a proxy in the absence of accrual data on other accounts payable.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2176,
      "end_char": 2367,
      "text": "3/ Insurance, Pension, and Standardized Guarantee Schemes, typically including government employee pension liabilities.\n4/ Includes accrual recording, commitment basis, due for payment, etc.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2367,
      "end_char": 2509,
      "text": "5/ Nominal value at any moment in time is the amount the debtor owes to the creditor. It reflects the value of the instrument at creation and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2509,
      "end_char": 2661,
      "text": "subsequent economic flows (such as transactions, exchange rate, and other valuation changes other than market price changes, and other\nvolume changes).\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2661,
      "end_char": 2894,
      "text": "6/ The face value of a debt instrument is the undiscounted amount of principal to be paid at (or before) maturity.\n7/ Market value of debt instruments is the value as if they were acquired in market transactions on the balance sheet "
